[rexglue-native] SDK 0313, released in setup tool 2.31.0 (2026-11-04): right-sized native render targets
(Vulkan; only with native_render_targets on). Draft name 0310 (drafts/0310-native-render-targets-right-sized
.UNTESTED.patch, 50cba0ef). New setting native_render_targets_right_sized (GPU, default off, read at start).
Off, nothing changes; xenos mode is not affected.

A native render target without MSAA is made only as tall as the draw it's made for may write (its scissor,
and with clipping its viewport, rounded up to 64 rows) instead of the whole EDRAM below its base
(1920x2736 or 1280x4096 at 32bpp, about 20 MiB times the scale squared). When a later draw, native resolve
or resolve clear needs more rows, a taller image of the same key replaces it (old rows copied, new rows
cleared as a new target starts; every pointer to it stays valid; the old image is freed once the GPU is done
with it). Targets grow, never shrink; a growth costs a one-off few milliseconds. MSAA targets and formats
that can't be copied keep the full height; anything that fails takes the old path and is logged.

Tested (R5-RELEASE-CANDIDATE.md): saint_lo at 1x, 2x, 3x and 4-player mp_merv at 2x, 0 errors, the Vulkan
validation layer with sync validation showing no new id.

